<title>USA: OPTIONS - Dollar vols hit after Rubin, employment.</title>
<headline>OPTIONS - Dollar vols hit after Rubin, employment.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Short-dated dollar-pair implied volatilities slid Friday as traders bailed out of positions following the U.S. jobs report and Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin's one-day visit to Japan.</p>
<p>Rubin's dollar-friendly comments sent the U.S. currency up a full yen overnight, but that was not enough of a jump to clear 125 yen and therefore not enough to pump up volatility, options analysts said.</p>
</text>
